  "case_id": "AMD-01",
  "title": "Handwritten carbon cash bill with struck-through corrections and a no-year date",
  "what_this_tests": "Two hazards that arrive together on real market chits. The date box prints 5/7/26 - 2026-07-05 under the GCC day-first rule, 2026-05-07 read American-style - and nothing else on the page disambiguates it, so the deterministic day-first derivation (WP-27) is the only correct reader. Two cells are struck through and rewritten; the corrected figures reconcile to 402.00 and the struck ones do not, so reading the wrong figure of a corrected pair shows up immediately in reconciliation.",
